  <description>The Berghof (German pronunciation: [ˈbɛʁkhoːf]) was Adolf Hitler's holiday retreat in the Obersalzberg of the Bavarian Alps near Berchtesgaden, Bavaria, Germany. Originally a modest chalet, Hitler holidayed there in the 1920s before purchasing it in 1933 with proceeds from Mein Kampf and significantly expanding it.</description>
